      "content": "The database connection is persistently denied (authentication error), so I cannot execute verification queries. I'll finalize based on the comprehensive semantic-network evidence, which includes exact precedent SQL for both halves of this composite question.\n\n---\n\n## Report\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (all 5 gold tables investigated):**\n- **LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: Subjects offered per term in library reserve scope; one row per subject per term. Key columns: `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID`, `SUBJECT_TITLE`, `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`, `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (\"Number of students enrolled in the subject per library records\").\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS**: Academic term dimension, one row per term. Key columns: `TERM_CODE`, `TERM_START_DATE`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `TERM_DESCRIPTION`.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED**: Section-level registrar offering fact table, one row per subject section per term. Key columns: `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID`, `OFFER_DEPT_CODE/NAME`, enrollment numbers at section/subject/cluster level.\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: Textbook Information Program subject offerings, one row per subject per term. Key columns: `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_TITLE`, `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` (\"joins to STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"), `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (\"used for enrollment-based rankings and window statistics\").\n- **STUDENT_DEPARTMENT**: Department lookup, one row per department: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME`, `SCHOOL_CODE`, `SCHOOL_NAME`.\n\n**Metrics (precedents retrieved in full):** `dw_4640`, `dw_5103`, `dw_4405`, `dw_4515`, `dw_4683`, `dw_3632` (SQL retrieved for all six).\n\n**Concepts:** `concept_subject_offering_facts`, `concept_course_material_programs`, `concept_department_dimension`, `concept_academic_term_dimension`.\n**Column concepts:** `column_concept_enrollment_measures`, `column_concept_term_code`, `column_concept_subject_id`, `column_concept_department_name`, `column_concept_year_columns`.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\nGraph traversal confirmed: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED joins ACADEMIC_TERMS via TERM_CODE; TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED joins STUDENT_DEPARTMENT via `OFFER_DEPT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE` and ACADEMIC_TERMS via TERM_CODE; SUBJECT_OFFERED joins ACADEMIC_TERMS via TERM_CODE. All three offering tables belong to `concept_subject_offering_facts`; TIP/library also belong to `concept_course_material_programs` (linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE).\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences & Task Fitness\n\n3a. **Enrollment measure candidates**: `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (library reserve scope) vs `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (textbook program scope) vs `SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` (registrar). The task wording explicitly says \"enrolled students **in the library subject offered**\" for the >3 filter → LIBRARY table; and the column mapping confirms the window measure is TIP's.\n\n3b. **Fitness mapping**:\n- Filter `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 3` on library scope → LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED: SUPPORTED (column exists; mapping \"library subject offered: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\").\n- Academic year → ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR: SUPPORTED (join on TERM_CODE per given join keys).\n- Number of unique subjects offered → COUNT(DISTINCT SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID): SUPPORTED (mapping explicitly names SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID; join key ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE ↔ SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE).\n- Minimum start date of the term → MIN(ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_START_DATE): SUPPORTED.\n- Term '2017JA' subject details (title, enrolled, faculty, offering dept name) → TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED: SUPPORTED (mapping names TIP columns; precedent dw_4640/dw_5103 use exactly these).\n- Department full name, school name → STUDENT_DEPARTMENT: SUPPORTED via `OFFER_DEPT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE` (documented join in column desc and given join keys).\n- Window min → `MIN(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) OVER (ORDER BY DEPARTMENT_CODE ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING)`: SUPPORTED (mapping lists TIP.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS + STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE).\n\n3c. **Wording anchoring**: \"in that department\" links the two halves via department name (LIBRARY/TIP `OFFER_DEPT_NAME` — the mapping lists both for \"department name\"). \"window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department code\" anchors to STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE (only the TIP half joins STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, matching dw_4640 exactly).\n\n3d. **Precedent usage**: The 2017JA + window-min shape appears in 2 precedents (dw_4640, dw_5103), both using `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED JOIN STUDENT_DEPARTMENT ON OFFER_DEPT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE TERM_CODE='2017JA'` with `MIN(...) OVER (ORDER BY t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING)`. The dept-year stats shape (COUNT(DISTINCT SUBJECT_ID), grouped by dept name + academic year, enrollment-threshold filter) appears in dw_4405 and dw_4515; the composite \"stats JOIN detail ON department name\" pattern appears in dw_4515 and dw_4683.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nLIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED serves library-reserve enrollment questions (dw_3393, dw_3911, dw_4683); TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED serves textbook-program enrollment/window questions (dw_4640, dw_5103, dw_4405); SUBJECT_OFFERED serves section-level offering counts (dw_3632); ACADEMIC_TERMS enriches all with year/dates; STUDENT_DEPARTMENT provides full name/school attribution (dw_4640, dw_5103).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nAll Phase 1 entities investigated: 5 gold tables (semantic_get + semantic_graph neighbors), 6 precedent metrics (semantic_get with full SQL), 4 concepts and 5 column concepts (semantic_search desc + graph memberships). mysql_query was attempted 8 times; all failed with \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\" — database verification was impossible, so the SQL is grounded entirely in retrieved column definitions, documented join keys, and exact precedent SQL.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n6a/6b. Two CTEs joined on department name:\n- **Stats CTE**: `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED l JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t ON l.TERM_CODE = t.TERM_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED so ON t.TERM_CODE = so.TERM_CODE WHERE l.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 3 GROUP BY l.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, t.ACADEMIC_YEAR` → dept name, academic year, `COUNT(DISTINCT so.SUBJECT_ID)`, `MIN(t.TERM_START_DATE)` (exactly the given join keys).\n- **2017JA CTE**: verbatim dw_4640/dw_5103 pattern on TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED + STUDENT_DEPARTMENT with the ROWS 3 PRECEDING/1 FOLLOWING window ordered by DEPARTMENT_CODE.\n- Final join on department name; SELECT list = the 11 requested columns in order.\n\n6c. **Data**: all required columns physically exist per retrieved definitions; joins use documented keys (TERM_CODE; OFFER_DEPT_CODE↔DEPARTMENT_CODE). **Semantic-network**: concept memberships and the given join keys match exactly. **Business**: two exact-shape precedents (dw_4640, dw_5103) plus composite-join precedents (dw_4515, dw_4683).\n\n6d. No tie-breakers needed — the column mapping and precedents uniquely determine every field.\n\n",
